A||||2||Oreif||1988 Coupe Suspension Question.||||5||
Z||000000||Oreif||06-09-2001||01:02 AM||||Hey all you 88 coupe guys. A friend is looking to buy an 88 coupe and wants to change the wheels. The question is:<BR>Does the original wheels on an 88 coupe have the different offset between front and rear wheels like the Formula and the GT? My guess would be that the suspensions are basically the same except for spring rates and the rear swaybar so the difference in the front/rear offset would be the same. What came stock on the 88 coupes?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||06-09-2001||01:26 AM||||The orignal wheels on my 88 coupe were all 4 the same, just 14 inch tech wheels. From what I know the suspention on all 88s were the same except for springs, shocks and sway bars. I put a new pair of 16 inch wheels and tires from tirerack on recently. I have 225/50WR-16 on the back and 205/55WR-16 on the front. The 16 inch wheels real look nice, not to big or small. The offset isnt really noticable now unless its pointed out. Also having the larger series tire on the back of the car helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||06-09-2001||02:01 AM||||Same here, I was running 87 GT rims w 205/60/15 on mine, and it was very noticable (see pics at site below).  I now have 16" GTZ rims with 225/50 rear and 205/50 front. And its not that bad.  I just picked up a swaybar and I have a set of KYBs and poly going on soon.  I plan to cut the springs, (changing the rate) and someday doing an engine swap.   Other than the engine and spring rates it is a good fake Formula. <P> I put the original 14" Turbo rims from my 88 on my 87 coupe and they fit it perfect, I think that the 14" are the same all the way around not like the GT 15" crosslace rims which were 15x6 (front) and 15x7 (rear).<P>Rob<P>I need to put new pics on my website, I have made too many changes since the pics were taken.<BR>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents. <A HREF="http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html</A>  <A HREF="http://vafiero.com" TARGET=_blank>http://vafiero.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||1
